  "hindi": "हे पूषन्, तुम्हारे लिए वषट्। इस प्रसव में अर्यमा, होता और विधाता कर्म करें। ऋत के अनुसार प्रसव करने वाली नारी शिथिल हो जाए, उसके जोड़ प्रसव के लिए खुल जाएँ।",
  "english": "Vaṣaṭ to you, O Pūṣan. In this birthing let Aryaman, the hotṛ priest, the ordainer, do the work. Let the woman, duly delivered, relax; let her joints open apart for the bearing.",
  "text_flags": [],
  "notes": "Src 'sūtavā ṷ' is sūtavai (Vedic infinitive) + u before a vowel (Devanagari सूत॒वा उ॑); the token ṷ is the particle u. Src 'sūtāv' with ṷ̄ is a transliteration artefact for ū/u. 'ṛta-prajātā' literally 'born/delivered in due order'; sense uncertain. Pūṣan, Aryaman are names of deities; hotṛ is a priest title, here an epithet of Aryaman by apposition. jihatām: form as printed, taken from √hā 'open'.",
  "confidence": "medium"
